<title>UK: TABLE-Courts yr profits surge 56.5 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Courts yr profits surge 56.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)(pre-exceps) 25.40		 vs  15.03</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   2.75		 vs   2.16</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)   3.75		 vs   3.00</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excepts	28.2		  vs  18.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   424.4		  vs 335.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Pretax profits before an exceptional credit of 1.2 million stg (versus 4.7 million) increased by 56.5 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;In the British Isles trading in the new financial year so far is showing like-for-like growth,&quot; said chief executive Bruce Cohen. &quot;However, after the rapid growth achieved in 1996/97 it has not been possible to maintain the same growth rate into 1997/98. The increased activity in the housing market and the windfall gains for many potential customers should lead to enhanced opportunities for Courts during the coming months&quot;.</p>
<p>Full name of furniture retailer - Courts Plc.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
